+● The review confirmed 4 findings (two are the same root cause). All are genuine, evidence-backed, and none contradict the passing tests:
+
+  1. page overflow → HTTP 500 (medium, found by 2 lenses) — a huge page like 99999999999999999999 makes offset exceed int64, SQLite throws SQLITE_MISMATCH → uncaught 500. Untrusted input causing a 5xx is a real
+  robustness defect.
+  2. Unconditional rebuild on every open (low, efficiency) — re-tokenizes the whole index on every startup for persisted DBs (~110ms/50k rows); should only backfill when the index was just created.
+  3. Repeated ?q=a&q=b → misleading 400 (nit) — Express parses it as an array, asString returns '', so a present param is rejected as "required".
