+  routes.ts was untouched — sync is fully declarative via triggers.
+
+  Key design decisions
+
+  - Ranking: bm25(notes_fts) with ORDER BY rank (ascending = most relevant first).
+  - Snippets: snippet(notes_fts, -1, '<mark>', '</mark>', …) — the -1 auto-selects the matching column, so a title-only hit is still highlighted.
+  - Injection-safe queries: input is tokenized (\p{L}\p{N}) and every token wrapped in double quotes, so FTS5 operators/punctuation in untrusted input can never throw a syntax error. Double-quoted spans become exact
+  phrases; the suggest endpoint makes the last token a prefix ("tok"*).
+
+  Adversarial review → 3 hardening fixes applied
+
+  A multi-lens review workflow (14 agents, findings adversarially verified with live probes) confirmed 4 real findings beyond the test suite; 5 raw findings were refuted as false positives. Fixes:
+  1. page overflow → 500 — a huge ?page= overflowed int64 and threw SQLITE_MISMATCH. Now clamped (MAX_PAGE), returns 200.
+  2. Unconditional rebuild — re-tokenized the whole index on every open; now backfills only when the index is newly created over a populated table.
+  3. Repeated ?q=a&q=b — was rejected with a misleading 400; now searches the first value.
+
+  All three were re-verified against the running app, and the full suite remains green.
